A company is starting an internal DVD lending service. All employees can list their DVDs on this service and borrow from each other. I may own several of one DVD, and someone else could own the same DVD as me. I want to keep track of who is lending which DVD to whom.
Identify that there may be more than one identical DVD in the library, and separate data about films from data about the physical copy of the DVD.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Employees (EmployeeID, EmailId, FirstName, LastName)
DVDMovies (MovieID, Title, GenreID, ReleaseYear)
Genres (GenreID, GenreName) - index on GenreName is good to have.
DVDInstances (DVDInstanceID, MovieID, OwnerEmployeeId, CurrentEmployeeId)
Transactions (TransactionID, DVDInstanceID, OwnerEmployeeID, BorrowerEmployeeID, BorrowDate, TentativeReturnDate, ActualReturnDate)

====================================================================================

Appropriate indices - look for forward thinking to identify how this data might reasonably be queried.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

